{"task_id": "HumanEval/4", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input conditions.\n    It provides a descriptive message for the error.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef mean_absolute_deviation(numbers: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of input numbers, calculate Mean Absolute Deviation\n    around the mean of this dataset.\n    MAD is the average absolute difference between each element and the dataset's mean.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    # Calculate the arithmetic mean of the numbers.\n    mean = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n\n    # Calculate the absolute difference between each number and the mean.\n    absolute_differences = [abs(x - mean) for x in numbers]\n\n    # Calculate the average of these absolute differences.\n    mad = sum(absolute_differences) / len(numbers)\n    return mad\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/7", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef filter_by_substring(strings: List[str], substring: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of strings, returning only those that contain the given substring.\n    Raises TypeError if inputs are not of the expected types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(strings, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'strings' must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(s, str) for s in strings):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'strings' must be strings.\")\n    if not isinstance(substring, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'substring' must be a string.\")\n\n    return [s for s in strings if substring in s]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _calculate_max_depth(group_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting depth for a single parenthesis group.\n    It iterates through characters, tracking current and maximum depths.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_depth = 0\n    current_depth = 0\n    for char in group_string:\n        if char == '(':\n            current_depth += 1\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, current_depth)\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_depth -= 1\n    return max_depth\n\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Input is a string of multiple space-separated groups of nested parentheses.\n    This function returns a list of the deepest nesting level for each group.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(paren_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n    results = []\n    for group in groups:\n        results.append(_calculate_max_depth(group))\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/4", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef mean_absolute_deviation(numbers: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Mean Absolute Deviation for a list of numbers.\n    Raises ValueError if the list is empty or TypeError for non-numeric elements.\"\"\"\n\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n    \n    # Validate all elements are numbers (int or float) as per design specification.\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    # Calculate the arithmetic mean of the input numbers.\n    mean_value = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n    \n    # Calculate the absolute differences between each number and the mean.\n    absolute_differences = [abs(num - mean_value) for num in numbers]\n    \n    # Calculate the arithmetic mean of these absolute differences.\n    mad_value = sum(absolute_differences) / len(absolute_differences)\n    \n    return mad_value\n```"}
