{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the greatest common divisor of two non-negative integers.\n    Uses the Euclidean algorithm and handles edge cases for zero inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, int) or not isinstance(b, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs must be integers\")\n    if a < 0 or b < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be non-negative integers\")\n\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return 0\n    if a == 0:\n        return b\n    if b == 0:\n        return a\n\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "```python\ndef greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Return a greatest common divisor of two integers a and b\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(3, 5)\n    1\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n```"}
