{"task_id": "HumanEval/18", "solution": "```python\ndef how_many_times(string: str, substring: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Find how many times a given substring can be found in the original string. Count overlaping cases.\n    >>> how_many_times('', 'a')\n    0\n    >>> how_many_times('aaa', 'a')\n    3\n    >>> how_many_times('aaaa', 'aa')\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    if not substring:\n        return 0\n    if not string:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate through the string to find all potential starting positions of the substring.\n    # Overlapping occurrences are counted by checking each possible start index.\n    for i in range(len(string) - len(substring) + 1):\n        if string[i:i+len(substring)] == substring:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/18", "solution": "```python\ndef how_many_times(string: str, substring: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of times a substring appears in a string, counting overlapping instances.\n    Returns 0 if the substring is empty or not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not substring:\n        return 0\n    \n    count = 0\n    # Iterate through the string, considering all possible start positions for the substring.\n    for i in range(len(string) - len(substring) + 1):\n        if string[i:i + len(substring)] == substring:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\n# This dictionary defines the mapping from musical note symbols to their beat durations.\n# It centralizes the constants as described in the design specification.\nNOTE_BEAT_MAP: Dict[str, int] = {\n    'o': 4,   # Whole note, lasts four beats.\n    'o|': 2,  # Half note, lasts two beats.\n    '.|': 1   # Quarter note, lasts one beat.\n}\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a specialized ASCII musical notation string into a sequence of beat durations.\n    It maps 'o' to 4 beats, 'o|' to 2 beats, and '.|' to 1 beat.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not music_string.strip():\n        return []\n\n    # Splits the music string into individual note symbols based on single spaces.\n    notes = music_string.split(' ')\n    beat_durations: List[int] = []\n\n    for note in notes:\n        if note in NOTE_BEAT_MAP:\n            beat_durations.append(NOTE_BEAT_MAP[note])\n        else:\n            # Raises a ValueError if an unknown note symbol is encountered, as per requirements.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown note symbol: '{note}'\")\n    return beat_durations\n```\n"}
