{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Decomposes a positive integer into its prime factors, listed in ascending order with correct multiplicity.\n    The product of the returned factors equals the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return []\n\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n\n    return factors\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep order of elements left the same as in the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(numbers)\n    result = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep order of elements left the same as in the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if any(not isinstance(x, int) for x in numbers):\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements in the input list must be integers.\")\n\n    counts = collections.Counter(numbers)\n    duplicates_to_remove = {num for num, count in counts.items() if count > 1}\n\n    result = [num for num in numbers if num not in duplicates_to_remove]\n    return result\n```"}
