{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int) or x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number 'x' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    min_allowed_base = 2\n    max_allowed_base = 9\n    if not isinstance(base, int) or not (min_allowed_base <= base <= max_allowed_base):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Base must be an integer between {min_allowed_base} and {max_allowed_base}.\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result_digits = []\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n    \n    return \"\".join(result_digits[::-1])\n```"}
