{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to Fib4 calculation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass Fib4Service:\n    \"\"\"Service to calculate Fib4 numbers efficiently using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n\n    FIB4_BASE_CASES: List[int] = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the Fib4Service with base cases.\"\"\"\n        self._cache: List[int] = list(self.FIB4_BASE_CASES)\n\n    def calculate(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fib4 number using dynamic programming.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if n is negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n        if n < len(self._cache):\n            return self._cache[n]\n\n        # Calculate iteratively and extend the cache\n        for i in range(len(self._cache), n + 1):\n            next_fib4 = (\n                self._cache[i - 1]\n                + self._cache[i - 2]\n                + self._cache[i - 3]\n                + self._cache[i - 4]\n            )\n            self._cache.append(next_fib4)\n\n        return self._cache[n]\n\n# Public function for direct use\n# A singleton-like instance allows the cache to persist across calls, improving efficiency.\n_fib4_service_instance = Fib4Service()\n\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n   