{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input during median calculation.\n    It carries a descriptive message about the error.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    This function validates input and handles odd/even length lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'l' must be a list.\")\n\n    if not l:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list must contain only numeric elements (int or float).\")\n\n    # Sort the list to find the median value.\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For odd length lists, the median is the middle element.\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # For even length lists, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for a given integer `n`, sorted ascending with multiplicities.\n    The product of these factors equals the absolute value of `n`.\n    >>> factorize(8)\n    [2, 2, 2]\n    >>> factorize(25)\n    [5, 5]\n    >>> factorize(70)\n    [2, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n    if n in (0, 1):\n        return []\n    \n    abs_n = abs(n)\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = abs_n\n\n    # Efficiently finds prime factors using trial division, accounting for multiplicities.\n    # Factors are added in ascending order, ensuring the final list is sorted.\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n    \n    return factors\n```"}
