{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef encode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes the input string by shifting each lowercase English alphabet character by 5 positions forward.\n    Non-lowercase characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    encoded_chars = []\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            shifted_char = chr(((ord(ch) + SHIFT_AMOUNT - ord(\"a\")) % 26) + ord(\"a\"))\n            encoded_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        else:\n            encoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string previously encoded by `encode_shift` by shifting each lowercase English alphabet character backward by 5 positions.\n    Non-lowercase characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            # Handle negative result of modulo correctly in Python to wrap around 'a' to 'z'.\n            shifted_char = chr(((ord(ch) - SHIFT_AMOUNT - ord(\"a\")) % 26 + 26) % 26 + ord(\"a\"))\n            decoded_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates 2^n modulo p using binary exponentiation.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(p, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Inputs n and p must be integers.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if p <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"p must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    res = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            res = (res * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n    return res\n```"}
