{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\nclass FruitParser:\n    # Responsibility: To extract numerical counts of specific fruits from a string.\n    def _extract_count(self, text: str, fruit_name: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Extracts the integer count for a specific fruit name from the text.\n        Returns 0 if the count is not found or cannot be parsed as an integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Matches one or more digits (\\d+) preceding the fruit name, case-insensitively.\n        pattern = rf\"(\\d+)\\s+{re.escape(fruit_name)}\\b\" # Added \\b for word boundary\n        match = re.search(pattern, text, re.IGNORECASE)\n        if match:\n            try:\n                return int(match.group(1))\n            except ValueError:\n                return 0\n        return 0\n\n    def parse_fruit_counts(self, s: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses the input string to find counts of apples and oranges.\n        Returns a dictionary with \"apples\" and \"oranges\" keys.\n        \"\"\"\n        apples = self._extract_count(s, \"apples\")\n        oranges = self._extract_count(s, \"oranges\")\n        return {\"apples\": apples, \"oranges\": oranges}\n\nclass FruitCalculator:\n    # Responsibility: To orchestrate parsing and calculate the final number of mangoes.\n    def calculate_mangoes(self, s: str, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the number of mangoes based on a string describing other fruits and a total count.\n        It uses FruitParser and ensures the returned mango count is non-negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = FruitParser()\n        fruit_counts = parser.parse_fruit_counts(s)\n\n        apples = fruit_counts.get(\"apples\", 0)\n        oranges = fruit_counts.get(\"oranges\", 0)\n\n        total_other_fruits = apples + oranges\n        raw_mangoes = n - total_other_fruits\n        return max(0, raw_mangoes)\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of mango fruits in a basket.\n    Given a string detailing apples and oranges and a total fruit count, it returns the non-negative mango count.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = FruitCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate_mangoes(s, n)\n\n```"}
