{"task_id": "HumanEval/68", "solution": "```python\ndef pluck(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the smallest even-valued node and its index from an array.\n    Returns [value, index] or an empty list if no even nodes are found or the array is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return []\n\n    smallest_even_value = None\n    smallest_even_index = -1\n\n    for index, value in enumerate(arr):\n        if value % 2 == 0:  # Check if the value is even.\n            if smallest_even_value is None or value < smallest_even_value:\n                smallest_even_value = value\n                smallest_even_index = index\n            # If value == smallest_even_value, we do nothing to keep the smallest index.\n\n    if smallest_even_value is not None:\n        return [smallest_even_value, smallest_even_index]\n    else:\n        return []\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/68", "solution": "```python\ndef pluck(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the smallest even-valued node and its index in an array.\n    If multiple nodes share the smallest even value, the one with the smallest index is chosen.\n    \"\"\"\n    smallest_even_value = float('inf')\n    smallest_even_index = -1\n\n    if not arr:\n        return []\n\n    for i, value in enumerate(arr):\n        # Constraints mention non-negative integers, and 0 is considered even.\n        if value % 2 == 0:\n            if value < smallest_even_value:\n                smallest_even_value = value\n                smallest_even_index = i\n            elif value == smallest_even_value and i < smallest_even_index:\n                # Update index if values are equal but the current index is smaller.\n                smallest_even_index = i\n\n    if smallest_even_index != -1:\n        # An even value was found, return its value and index.\n        return [smallest_even_value, smallest_even_index]\n    else:\n        # No even values were found in the array.\n        return []\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/69", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef search(lst: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the greatest integer in `lst` with frequency >= its value.\n    Returns -1 if no such integer exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequencies = Counter(lst)\n\n    candidates = []\n    for num, freq in frequencies.items():\n        if freq >= num:\n            candidates.append(num)\n\n    if not candidates:\n        return -1\n    \n    return max(candidates)\n```"}
