{"task_id": "HumanEval/73", "solution": "```python\ndef smallest_change(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array arr of integers, find the minimum number of elements that\n    need to be changed to make the array palindromic. In one change, you can change one element to any other element.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n\n    changes = 0\n    left_ptr = 0\n    right_ptr = n - 1\n\n    while left_ptr < right_ptr:\n        if arr[left_ptr] != arr[right_ptr]:\n            changes += 1\n        left_ptr += 1\n        right_ptr -= 1\n    return changes\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/73", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidArrayError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid array inputs.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef smallest_change(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum changes needed to make the array palindromic.\n    Raises InvalidArrayError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise InvalidArrayError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    for item in arr:\n        if not isinstance(item, int):\n            raise InvalidArrayError(\"All elements in the array must be integers.\")\n\n    changes = 0\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    while left < right:\n        if arr[left] != arr[right]:\n            changes += 1\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return changes\n```"}
