{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"\n    Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'x' must be an integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(shift, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'shift' must be an integer.\")\n    if shift < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'shift' cannot be negative.\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    sign = \"-\" if x < 0 else \"\"\n    x_str = str(abs(x))\n    num_digits = len(x_str)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        # If shift > number of digits, digits are reversed.\n        result_str = x_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Perform circular right shift on digits.\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        result_str = x_str[-effective_shift:] + x_str[:-effective_shift]\n\n    return sign + result_str\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"\n    Circular shifts digits of x to the right, returning the result as a string.\n    If shift exceeds number of digits, it reverses digits instead.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_x = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(s_x)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        # If shift is greater than number of digits, reverse the string.\n        return s_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Perform circular right shift.\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        if effective_shift == 0:\n            return s_x\n        \n        # Split into suffix (last 'effective_shift' digits) and prefix, then concatenate.\n        suffix = s_x[num_digits - effective_shift:]\n        prefix = s_x[:num_digits - effective_shift]\n        return suffix + prefix\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/80", "solution": "```python\ndef is_happy(s):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string is \\\"happy\\\": its length is at least 3 and every 3 consecutive letters are distinct.\n    Returns True if the string is happy, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    MIN_HAPPY_STRING_LENGTH = 3\n\n    if len(s) < MIN_HAPPY_STRING_LENGTH:\n        return False\n\n    # Check every sliding window of 3 characters for distinctness.\n    for i in range(len(s) - (MIN_HAPPY_STRING_LENGTH - 1)):\n        # If any two characters in the window are the same, they are not distinct.\n        if s[i] == s[i+1] or s[i] == s[i+2] or s[i+1] == s[i+2]:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
