{"task_id": "HumanEval/85", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the calculation function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef add(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all even elements located at odd indices in a list.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for empty or non-integer lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n    \n    # Validate all elements are integers as per FR1.\n    for item in lst:\n        if not isinstance(item, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list must contain only integers.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through the list with 0-based index.\n    for i, num in enumerate(lst):\n        # Check if the index is odd (1, 3, 5, ...) and the number is even.\n        if i % 2 != 0 and num % 2 == 0:\n            total_sum += num\n            \n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(N):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\n    \n    Example\n        For N = 1000, the sum of digits will be 1 the output should be \"1\".\n        For N = 150, the sum of digits will be 6 the output should be \"110\".\n        For N = 147, the sum of digits will be 12 the output should be \"1100\".\n    \n    Variables:\n        @N integer\n             Constraints: 0 \u2264 N \u2264 10000.\n    Output:\n         a string of binary number\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Validate the input N according to requirements.\n    if not isinstance(N, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input N must be an integer.\")\n    if not (0 <= N <= 10000):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input N must be between 0 and 10000 (inclusive).\")\n    \n    decimal_sum = 0\n    temp_n = N\n    # Calculate the sum of decimal digits for N.\n    if temp_n == 0:\n        decimal_sum = 0\n    else:\n        while temp_n > 0:\n            decimal_sum += temp_n % 10\n            temp_n //= 10\n    \n    # Convert the calculated decimal_sum to its binary string representation.\n    if decimal_sum == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    \n    binary_string = \"\"\n    temp_num = decimal_sum\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        binary_string = str(temp_num % 2) + binary_string\n        temp_num //= 2\n    return binary_string\n```"}
