{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "import re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns an ordered version of the input string `s`. Characters within each word are sorted by ASCII value, while preserving original word order and spacing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Split the string into words and space delimiters. The regex r'(\\s+)' captures whitespace, including it in the result list.\n    tokens = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n    result_tokens = []\n\n    for token in tokens:\n        # If the token is empty or consists only of spaces, it's a space delimiter or an artifact of splitting at boundaries.\n        if not token or token.strip() == \"\":\n            result_tokens.append(token)\n        else:\n            # Sort characters within the word based on their ASCII values.\n            result_tokens.append(\"\".join(sorted(token)))\n\n    return \"\".join(result_tokens)"}
