{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array of non-negative integers based on the parity of the sum of its first and last elements.\n    It returns a new sorted array, ensuring the original array remains unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    copied_array = list(array) # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original\n\n    if len(copied_array) == 1:\n        return copied_array\n\n    first_element = copied_array[0]\n    last_element = copied_array[-1]\n    sum_first_last = first_element + last_element\n\n    if sum_first_last % 2 != 0:  # Odd sum, sort ascending\n        copied_array.sort()\n    else:  # Even sum, sort descending\n        copied_array.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return copied_array\n```"}
