{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\nSHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypts a string by rotating alphabetic characters by a fixed shift amount.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged, and case is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            # Shift lowercase character, handling wrap-around.\n            base = ord('a')\n            shifted_char = chr(base + (ord(char) - base + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % 26)\n            encrypted_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            # Shift uppercase character, handling wrap-around.\n            base = ord('A')\n            shifted_char = chr(base + (ord(char) - base + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % 26)\n            encrypted_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        else:\n            # Preserve non-alphabetic characters.\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string by rotating alphabetic characters by a fixed shift of 4.\n    Non-alphabetic characters in the string remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n\n    def _is_lowercase(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is a lowercase English letter.\"\"\"\n        return 'a' <= char <= 'z'\n\n    def _is_uppercase(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is an uppercase English letter.\"\"\"\n        return 'A' <= char <= 'Z'\n\n    def _rotate_char(char: str, shift: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Rotates an alphabetic character by the shift amount, preserving case and wrapping.\"\"\"\n        if _is_lowercase(char):\n            start = ord('a')\n            return chr(start + (ord(char) - start + shift) % 26)\n        elif _is_uppercase(char):\n            start = ord('A')\n            return chr(start + (ord(char) - start + shift) % 26)\n        return char\n\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n        \n    encrypted_chars = [_rotate_char(char, SHIFT_AMOUNT) for char in s]\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```\n"}
