{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a number string and returns the closest integer, rounding away from zero for equidistant values (e.g., X.5).\n    For example, closest_integer(\"14.5\") returns 15, and closest_integer(\"-14.5\") returns -15.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_float = float(value)\n\n    if num_float == int(num_float):\n        return int(num_float)\n\n    floor_num = math.floor(num_float)\n    ceil_num = math.ceil(num_float)\n\n    diff_floor = abs(num_float - floor_num)\n    diff_ceil = abs(num_float - ceil_num)\n\n    if diff_floor == diff_ceil:  # Equidistant, e.g., X.5.\n        if num_float > 0:\n            return ceil_num  # Round up for positive numbers.\n        else:\n            return floor_num # Round down for negative numbers, away from zero.\n    elif diff_floor < diff_ceil:\n        return floor_num\n    else:\n        return ceil_num\n```"}
