{"task_id": "HumanEval/112", "solution": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string is a palindrome.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'text' must be a string.\")\n    return text == text[::-1]\n\ndef reverse_delete(s: str, c: str) -> tuple[str, bool]:\n    \"\"\"Deletes characters from 's' found in 'c' and checks if the result is a palindrome.\n    Returns a tuple (result_string, is_palindrome_flag).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str) or not isinstance(c, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs 's' and 'c' must be strings.\")\n\n    c_set = set(c)\n    s_prime_chars = []\n\n    for char_s in s:\n        if char_s not in c_set:\n            s_prime_chars.append(char_s)\n\n    s_prime = \"\".join(s_prime_chars)\n    is_palindrome_result = is_palindrome(s_prime)\n\n    return (s_prime, is_palindrome_result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/110", "solution": "```python\ndef exchange(lst1, lst2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if it's possible to make lst1 contain only even numbers by exchanging elements with lst2.\n    This is possible if lst2 has enough even numbers to replace all odd numbers in lst1.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count_lst1 = sum(1 for x in lst1 if x % 2 != 0)\n    even_count_lst2 = sum(1 for x in lst2 if x % 2 == 0)\n\n    if even_count_lst2 >= odd_count_lst1:\n        return \"YES\"\n    else:\n        return \"NO\"\n```"}
