{"task_id": "HumanEval/145", "solution": "```python\ndef _sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the absolute digits of an integer.\n    Handles negative numbers by using their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = 0\n    n_abs = abs(n)\n    if n_abs == 0:\n        return 0\n    while n_abs > 0:\n        s += n_abs % 10\n        n_abs //= 10\n    return s\n\ndef order_by_points(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers by the sum of their digits in ascending order.\n    Ties are broken by the original index of the integers in the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return []\n\n    decorated_list = []\n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        decorated_list.append((_sum_digits(num), i, num))\n\n    decorated_list.sort()\n\n    sorted_nums = [item[2] for item in decorated_list]\n    return sorted_nums\n```"}
