{"task_id": "HumanEval/122", "solution": "```python\ndef add_elements(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of elements with at most two digits from the first k elements of arr.\n    An element qualifies if its absolute value is between 0 and 99, inclusive.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through the first k elements of the array.\n    for i in range(k):\n        element = arr[i]\n        # Include the element in the sum if its absolute value is 99 or less.\n        if -99 <= element <= 99:\n            current_sum += element\n    return current_sum\n```"}
